{
  "email": "leo.martins@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify sender, department/title, and laptop for software request per KB-027"
}

{
  "query": "Zoom Company Portal approved apps",
  "reason": "Check whether Zoom is an approved Company Portal app"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, thanks for reaching out, and happy to help you get ready for tomorrow's client meeting. First, please open the Company Portal (Software Center) on your laptop and search for \"Zoom\". If it's listed, click Install. You don't need IT for that, and it only takes a few minutes. If Zoom isn't there, it will need your manager's approval and a security review before we can install it. In that case, reply to this ticket and include your manager's name, and ask your manager to reply here approving the Zoom install for client meetings. We'll pass it on as soon as that approval comes in. Since the meeting is tomorrow and the review may not be finished in time, it's also worth asking the client whether they could send a Teams invite instead. Please don't install Zoom from a download link you got by email. Just let us know what you find in the Company Portal.",
  "internal_note": "P4 software request (KB-027). Sender: Leo Martins (user_id 6), Sales, Account Executive, laptop BL-LT-0106, account active and in good standing. None of my tools can check what's in the Company Portal, so I asked the user to look for Zoom there first. A KB search found no article saying whether Zoom is pre-approved. If it isn't in the Portal, it needs manager approval and a security review. Once the manager approves, escalate to Tier 2 with: app Zoom (current version), business reason 'client meetings (Sales)', and the approver's name. I didn't install anything and didn't grant admin rights.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-027"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
